@startuml browser_masquerade_sequence
' Browser masquerade search workflow with measured timings (2026-09-26).
' 6 lanes on Xvfb :99-:104, distro Chromium 154, Thai residential egress.

autonumber

participant "Onyx\n(web_search tool)" as Onyx
participant "searxng\nwebapp" as Web
participant "engine module\n(google/bing/brave)" as Eng
participant "BrowserFetchPool\n(6 lanes)" as Pool
participant "lane N\nChromium on Xvfb" as Lane
participant "human_input\n(XTEST pointer)" as Hand
participant "captcha_vision\n(OpenAI-compatible\nvision endpoint)" as Vision
participant "provider\n(google.com ...)" as Up

Onyx -> Web : GET /search?q=... (json)
note right of Onyx : Onyx client read budget 90 s\n(SEARXNG_READ_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)

Web -> Eng : engine request
Eng -> Pool : fetch(url) via browser pool
note right of Pool : provider send pacing:\n1-5 s random gap per host,\nqueue cap 20 s

Pool -> Pool : checkout next idle lane\n(asyncio lane cycle)
note right of Pool : wait here if all 6 lanes busy\n(engine timeout budget:\ngoogle 85 s, others 60 s)

alt maximum stealth (browser_max_stealth: on)
    Pool -> Lane : open provider homepage\n(hl/gl locale params ride along)
    Lane -> Up : GET homepage
    Hand -> Lane : Bezier move to search box (0.04-0.10 s),\nreal click focuses the box
    Hand -> Lane : type query with human cadence\n(uneven keys, bursts, pauses)
    Hand -> Lane : drift pointer (0.4-1.4 s),\nclick the submit button
    Lane -> Up : form submit -> results page
    Pool -> Lane : settle: wait for navigation,\nread results like a human
    note right of Pool : full human search measured ~19 s\n(warm lane, google)

    opt challenge served (/sorry or 200 CAPTCHA wall)
        Pool -> Lane : screenshot challenge + instruction text
        loop up to 12 rounds (max_rounds)
            loop 6 votes (votes), rising temperature
                Lane -> Vision : screenshot + prompt (~35 s per vote,\nendpoint timeout 360 s)
                Vision --> Lane : tile coordinates
                Hand -> Lane : click tiles with real X input
            end
            Hand -> Lane : press VERIFY (strict-majority quorum)
            opt rejected -> grid regrows
                Lane -> Lane : next round, adapted geometry
            end
        end
        note right of Lane : a round costs ~3.5-4 min;\n12 rounds ~50 min worst case.\nA request waiting on a solve\ngives up at its engine timeout,\nthe lane keeps solving in the\nbackground and banks the\nclearance cookies
    end

    Pool -> Lane : capture rendered DOM (google desktop layout)
    Lane --> Pool : HTML (~2.9 MB)
    Pool --> Eng : response
    Eng -> Eng : parse results\n(/url?q= unwrapped,\n/goto?url= kept as absolute URL)
else not a human-search candidate (API endpoints, images, ddg)
    Pool -> Lane : fetch-style request in browser context\n(browser TLS + lane cookies)
    Lane -> Up : GET url
    Lane --> Pool : response
end

opt post-search browsing (browser_post_search_browsing)\nonly when another lane is idle
    Pool -> Lane : background task keeps the SERP page
    loop 1-4 visits, budget 180 s total
        Hand -> Lane : click an organic result\n(/goto wrapper -> new tab; never\ntranslate.goog targets)
        Lane -> Up : navigate to result
        Hand -> Lane : scroll + pointer drift, dwell 10-30 s
        Lane -> Lane : close tab, back on results
    end
    note right of Lane : measured: 4 visits in 170 s
    Lane --> Pool : lane returns to the cycle
end

Pool --> Web : parsed results
Web --> Onyx : json (measured ~19-20 s warm,\nno challenge)
@enduml
